<title>USA: Ancor gets $600,000 Japan order.</title>
<headline>Ancor gets $600,000 Japan order.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ancor Communications Inc said Thursday it received an order in excess of $600,000 from Hucom Inc, its Japanese distributor, including more than $500,000 for Ancor GigWorks switches and adapters.</p>
<p>Ancor said Hucom will begin Phase II implementation of a $7.4 million Fibre Channel network now being installed for a major Japanese manufacturer at a new design and engineering facility.</p>
<p>This order follows a $1.5 million order announced in the fourth quarter, the company said.</p>
<p>Ancor provides communications network backbone products.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
